<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6129" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφιφορεύς</span></b> , gen. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">έως</span>, 
			Ep.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῆος</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, ὁ</span>:
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φέρω, φορέω</span>):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>large jar</i> or <i>pitcher with
				two handles,</i> of gold, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				23.92
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				24.74
			</span></i>; of stone, <i><span class="en">
				13.105
			</span></i>; for wine, <i><span class="en">
				2.290
			</span></i>, etc.; for oil, <i><span class="en">
				Simon.
				155.4
			</span></i>: used as <i>cinerary urn,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
			</span></i> l.c. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετρητής</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Theopomp.Hist.
				374
			</span></i>. (The later form was <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφορεύς,</span> q.v.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
